// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// T27 OS native_host (v0.3.0): where the native chat slice, the agent runner and the swarm coordinator
// touch the machine through libSystem. No decisions live here; every rule is a tested fn in native_provider
// (request bytes, reply parsing, error classes, the wait verdict), native_log (the append-only log, recovery),
// native_policy (tools, approval, env names), native_agent and native_swarm (the state machines).
//
// What this file does, and nothing else:
//   - reads the four LM Studio settings from the environment (T27OS_LMSTUDIO_HOST / _PORT / _MODEL / _API_KEY),
//     only those four names (native_policy env_name_known), and never prints or stores a value;
//   - one HTTP exchange with the loopback server over AF_INET (socket, connect, write, poll, read to EOF), with
//     a deadline and a cancel file checked at every poll slice;
//   - the durable log: the whole image is written to <name>.log.part, fsynced, closed and renamed over
//     <name>.log (the same order profile_host.t27 uses), so a crash leaves the old file or the new one;
//   - recovery: the image is read back and native_log keeps every complete event up to the first bad line;
//   - one chat turn on a session, one agent run, one swarm run (members one at a time).
//
// Not here, on purpose: DSH, NVIDIA, fallback between providers, key rotation, streaming (the call is a single
// non-streaming request that closes the connection after the reply), compaction of the log.
//
// A path passed to libSystem is a byte buffer with a 0 byte right after the last path byte; every path below is
// built by host_session_file into a zeroed buffer, which supplies it.
//
// Specs holding @extern cannot run under t27c; the pure rules are tested in their own specs, and this file's
// tests run under `t27b test specs/t27os/native_host.t27` (they need no LM Studio; the real call is in
// native_accept.t27).
//
// Refs gHashTag/t27#13212.
module T27osNativeHost;

